+# myrmidon(G1): a VACUUM writes the surviving data into a temporary database and then back into the
+# database file, so it needs about the live data twice: once in SQLite's temp directory, once as the rollback
+# journal (-journal; -wal in WAL mode) next to the database. These helpers decide, before the rewrite starts,
+# whether the volumes can take it.
